Title: DOCKS RUN
Author: ScriptLens Demo
Draft date: July 2026

FADE IN:

INT. ABANDONED WAREHOUSE - NIGHT

GINA VASQUEZ, 32, ex-driver, pries open a STEEL BRIEFCASE on a crate. Stacks of banded cash inside.

GINA
Still heavy. Good.

INT. RAIN-SLICK ALLEY - NIGHT

A lone MOTORCYCLE idles under a busted streetlight. The rider pulls away without a word.

INT. PARKING GARAGE - NIGHT

Gina slides the briefcase into her trunk. She checks a photo of the buyer taped to the lid.

GINA
One hour. No second stops.

INT. SAFEHOUSE - NIGHT

Two RIVALS block the door. The taller one taps the briefcase with a pistol.

RIVAL
Wrong night to move product, Gina.

GINA
Then get out of my lane.

EXT. DOCKS - NIGHT

Gina shoves the briefcase across a loading table. A BUYER nods and signals his crew.

BUYER
Clean handoff. We're done.

FADE OUT.

THE END
